    a: "<b>Green House Project:</b><ul><li>Transformational model of residential LTC developed by <b>Dr. Bill Thomas</b> (Eden Alternative founder)</li><li>Replaces traditional large nursing home with <b>small, intentional home</b></li></ul><b>Core Features:</b><ol><li><b>Small home size:</b> 7–12 residents per house (not a large institutional building)</li><li><b>Private rooms and bathrooms</b> for all residents</li><li><b>Open kitchen and hearth</b> — central social gathering space; cooking smells, shared meals</li><li><b>Shahbaz (universal worker)</b> — cross-trained direct care worker who provides personal care, cooks meals, facilitates activities; consistent assignment to specific residents</li><li><b>Clinical Guide (RN)</b> — provides nursing oversight without direct supervisory hierarchy over Shahbaz</li><li><b>Resident self-direction</b> — residents choose wake time, meals, activities; no institutional schedule</li><li><b>Elimination of nursing stations</b> and institutional paraphernalia</li></ol><b>Outcomes vs. Traditional NH:</b><ul><li>Better quality of life; higher resident and family satisfaction</li><li>Reduced antipsychotic use; fewer hospitalizations</li><li>Lower staff turnover</li><li>Higher construction cost but comparable operating cost</li></ul>"
