    a: "<b>HICAP (Health Insurance Counseling and Advocacy Program) / SHIP (State Health Insurance Assistance Program):</b><ul><li>Federally funded program providing <b>free, unbiased Medicare counseling</b> to beneficiaries and their families</li><li>Called HICAP in some states (CA, CO), SHIP in others — same program nationally</li><li>Funded by CMS; services provided by trained volunteer counselors</li></ul><b>Services Provided (All Free):</b><ol><li><b>Medicare plan selection</b> — comparing Original Medicare vs. Medicare Advantage; drug plan (Part D) selection</li><li><b>Medicare billing review</b> — reviewing Explanation of Benefits; identifying billing errors or potential fraud</li><li><b>Appeals assistance</b> — helping beneficiaries appeal claim denials (Medicare Part A, B, C, D)</li><li><b>Low-income subsidy (LIS/Extra Help)</b> enrollment — Part D premium assistance for low-income beneficiaries</li><li><b>Medicare Savings Programs</b> — QMB, SLMB, QI, QDWI programs that pay Part B premiums, copays, deductibles</li><li><b>Medicaid enrollment</b> assistance for dual-eligible beneficiaries</li><li><b>Medigap (supplemental insurance)</b> counseling</li></ol><b>Referral:</b> Contact local Area Agency on Aging; 1-800-Medicare; state SHIP website"
