    a: "<b>Community-Based Services for Parkinson's Disease with Dysphagia — Discharge Planning:</b><ol><li><b>Home health:</b><ul><li><b>Speech therapy</b> (skilled need for dysphagia management — swallowing exercises, LSVT LOUD if voice impairment, diet texture modification education)</li><li><b>Physical therapy</b> (gait training, fall prevention — LSVT BIG program)</li><li><b>Occupational therapy</b> (adaptive equipment for tremor: weighted utensils, tremor-dampening cups)</li><li><b>Skilled nursing</b> (medication management, Parkinson's disease monitoring)</li></ul></li><li><b>Modified diet:</b> Coordinate with dietitian and SLP for appropriate texture (IDDSI framework) and thickened liquids if indicated</li><li><b>Meals on Wheels</b> — modified texture meals delivered at home; reduces nutritional risk</li><li><b>Home health aide</b> — bathing, dressing (if caregiver needs support)</li><li><b>Durable Medical Equipment (DME):</b> Hospital bed, walker, shower chair, raised toilet seat</li><li><b>Caregiver education</b> — dysphagia precautions, medication timing, Parkinson's falls management</li><li><b>Parkinson's Foundation helpline</b> and local support group</li><li><b>Telehealth follow-up</b> with neurologist and primary care</li></ol>"
