    a: "<b>Geriatric Interdisciplinary Team (IDT) — Core Members and SDOH Roles:</b><ol><li><b>Geriatrician/Physician:</b> Medical diagnosis, medication management, goals of care, ACP facilitation, SDOH screening integration</li><li><b>Social Worker:</b> Comprehensive SDOH assessment, resource linkage, discharge planning, APS reporting, caregiver burden assessment, advance directive facilitation</li><li><b>Registered Nurse/Nurse Practitioner:</b> Medication education, wound care, disease management, transitional care coordination, home health ordering</li><li><b>Pharmacist:</b> Medication reconciliation, deprescribing, polypharmacy review, medication assistance programs (PAP)</li><li><b>Physical Therapist:</b> Mobility assessment, fall prevention programs, exercise prescription, home safety evaluation</li><li><b>Occupational Therapist:</b> ADL/IADL assessment, home modification recommendations, adaptive equipment, cognitive rehabilitation</li><li><b>Speech-Language Pathologist:</b> Dysphagia, communication, cognitive-communication disorders</li><li><b>Dietitian:</b> Nutritional assessment, malnutrition management, Meals on Wheels referral, modified texture diets</li><li><b>Chaplain/Spiritual Care:</b> Spiritual assessment, existential distress, end-of-life support</li><li><b>Community Health Worker:</b> SDOH navigation, resource linkage, home visiting, cultural liaison</li></ol><b>Model programs:</b> PACE IDT; Geriatric Evaluation and Management (GEM) programs; VA GRECC"
